<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="8765fa99">&lt;p&gt;
    Business Case calculates benefits of implementing improvement opportunities, additional costs that will need to be
    incurred, and required investments.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="8e292e62"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="92cc8c5e">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Confirm that the link is clear between the business case objectives, the activities that will deliver the
        benefits and the business impacts (financial and non-financial).
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Engage fully with stakeholders and subject matter experts to raise the quality of information in the business
        case.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="91b28fa3"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="706045f8">To justify an investment by explaining and quantifying the financial and non-financial benefits of a program or project and
capturing information pertaining to the realization of these benefits.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="6bb43814"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="d4656436"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="e0356edb">&lt;p&gt;
    A business case may contain the following sections:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Summary program or project information
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Overview of current state
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Key drivers for change
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Potential options - proposed future state options, benefits of each option, potentially a recommendation on
        selection
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Key business drivers and investment objectives
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Assumptions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Market data and industry benchmarks
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Other environmental factors impacting the need for change
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Problem or issue statement
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Scope and key activities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Key financial information
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Costs and benefits breakdown
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Investment appraisal calculations
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Strategic alignment
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Regulatory requirements
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Risk evaluation
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Critical dependencies
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Descriptions of intended benefits and owners for each
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Benefits measures
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        High-level timeline for benefits realization
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Resource requirements
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Cash flow forecast and discounted cash flow forecast
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Recommendations
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The business case content and level of detail depends on the specifics of the project and anticipated benefits and
    costs.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="64eec572">&lt;p&gt;
    The format of the business case presentation may differ by program or the expectations of the review group to which it
    will be presented.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representation" nodeId="440cdb52"></attribute>
